<article class="env-lemma" id="08QA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08QA">Lemma <span data-tag="08QA">21.39.8</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Example <a href="/tag/08PH" data-tag="08PH">21.39.3</a>. If there exists a cosimplicial object $U'_\bullet $ of $\mathcal{C}'$ such that Lemma <a href="/tag/08Q9" data-tag="08Q9">21.39.7</a> applies to both $U'_\bullet $ in $\mathcal{C}'$ and $u(U'_\bullet )$ in $\mathcal{C}$, then we have $L\pi '_! \circ g^{-1} = L\pi _!$ as functors $D(\mathcal{C}) \to D(\textit{Ab})$, resp. $D(\mathcal{C}, \underline{B}) \to D(B)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/08Q9" data-tag="08Q9">21.39.7</a> and the fact that $g^{-1}$ is given by precomposing with $u$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>